{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789384415,"nonce":"ntemdpy7ICIrDo34c/0zjt312Ws=","title":"Python: an annotated local took the value's type, not the annotation's","message":"`v: float = bag.payload` typed `v` as Object because the inference\ntyped an annotated assignment from its value alone; every operation on\n`v` then went through `zb_any_arith` on boxes, and `total = total + v`\nmade `total` a box too. `bench_any_field.py` spent 27 ms boxing and\ndispatching where ZynML's `let v: f64 = bag.payload` unboxes once.\n\nNow a dynamic value assigned to an annotated local takes the\nannotation, read back with the check a parameter's annotation gets\n(TypeError when it does not fit). A value whose type is already known\nkeeps it: `x: float = 3` still binds the int, as CPython does.\nConformance `inference/annotated_from_dynamic.py`.","files":null}]}